<h1>Leads</h1>

<p>
    The Leads area helps you track new business opportunities from first contact through conversion to a client. It's designed to keep your sales pipeline organized and visible.
</p>

<!-- IMAGE PLACEHOLDER: Full-page screenshot of the Leads board view showing multiple lead cards in different stages (New, Contacted, Qualified, Proposal, etc.). Show the swimlane layout with cards that can be dragged between stages. Include labels for the stage columns. -->

<h2>Board View</h2>

<p>
    The default view for leads is a board (also called a Kanban board) that organizes leads into stages. Each stage represents a step in your sales process.
</p>

<p>
    <strong>How it works:</strong>
</p>

<ul>
    <li><strong>Stages are columns</strong> – Each stage appears as a vertical column (like "New," "Contacted," "Qualified," "Proposal," "Won," "Lost")</li>
    <li><strong>Leads are cards</strong> – Each lead appears as a card in the appropriate stage</li>
    <li><strong>Drag to move</strong> – Click and drag a lead card to move it to a different stage as it progresses</li>
    <li><strong>Visual progress</strong> – You can see at a glance where each lead is in your process</li>
</ul>

<p>
    <strong>Show All option:</strong>
</p>

<p>
    By default, the board shows active leads. If you want to see closed leads (won or lost) as well, use the "Show All" option. This is helpful when you want to review the month's activity or see your conversion rates.
</p>

