<h2>Searching for Leads</h2>

<p>
    The search box at the top of the Leads page helps you find leads quickly. It searches across:
</p>

<ul>
    <li><strong>Company name</strong> – Find leads by business name</li>
    <li><strong>Contact name</strong> – Search by the contact person's name</li>
    <li><strong>Email address</strong> – Find leads by email</li>
    <li><strong>Phone number</strong> – Search by phone</li>
</ul>

<p>
    This is especially useful when you're on a call and need to quickly find a lead's information. Just type a few letters and the matching leads appear.
</p>

<!-- IMAGE PLACEHOLDER: Screenshot of the search box with a query typed in (e.g., "Acme") showing matching leads in the results. Highlight the search box and show the filtered results. -->

<h2>Recent Activity</h2>

<p>
    Each lead has a recent activity list that shows the last interactions and updates. This helps you:
</p>

<ul>
    <li><strong>See the story</strong> – Understand what's happened with this lead recently</li>
    <li><strong>Pick up where you left off</strong> – Know what the last touchpoint was</li>
    <li><strong>Track progress</strong> – See how the lead has moved through your process</li>
</ul>

<p>
    Click on a lead card or row to open the lead details and see the full activity history. You can also add new activities directly from the lead detail page.
</p>

<!-- IMAGE PLACEHOLDER: Screenshot of a lead detail page showing the recent activity section. Show a few example activities with timestamps and user names. Include an "Add Activity" button or similar. -->

<h2>List View</h2>

<p>
    In addition to the board view, you can switch to a list view that shows leads in a compact table format. This is useful when you need to:
</p>

<ul>
    <li><strong>See more leads at once</strong> – The table format shows more information in less space</li>
    <li><strong>Make bulk updates</strong> – Update multiple leads quickly</li>
    <li><strong>Export or review data</strong> – Easier to scan and work with large numbers of leads</li>
</ul>

<p>
    Switch between board and list views using the toggle in the sidebar or toolbar. Both views show the same leads, just organized differently.
</p>

