<h2>Working with Lead Details</h2>

<p>
    When you open a lead, you'll see:
</p>

<ul>
    <li><strong>Contact information</strong> – All the details about the company and contact person</li>
    <li><strong>Notes and history</strong> – Everything that's happened with this lead</li>
    <li><strong>Related items</strong> – Any policies, proposals, or other records connected to this lead</li>
    <li><strong>Activity timeline</strong> – A chronological view of all interactions</li>
</ul>

<p>
    You can edit the lead, add notes, log calls, attach files, and convert the lead to a client when they're ready.
</p>

<!-- IMAGE PLACEHOLDER: Screenshot of a lead detail page showing the main sections: contact info, notes, activity timeline, and action buttons. Use callouts to identify each section. -->

<h2>Converting Leads to Clients</h2>

<p>
    When a lead becomes a client, you can convert them directly from the lead record. This:
</p>

<ul>
    <li>Creates a new client record with all the lead's information</li>
    <li>Moves the lead to the "Won" stage (or marks it as converted)</li>
    <li>Preserves the lead's history so you can see how they became a client</li>
    <li>Allows you to start creating policies and renewals for the new client</li>
</ul>

<p>
    The conversion process is designed to be smooth so you don't lose any information in the transition.
</p>

<!-- IMAGE PLACEHOLDER: Screenshot showing the "Convert to Client" button or action on a lead detail page. Show a confirmation dialog or the conversion process. -->

<h2>Tips for Managing Leads</h2>

<ul>
    <li><strong>Keep stages updated</strong> – Move leads through stages as they progress so your board stays accurate</li>
    <li><strong>Add notes regularly</strong> – Log interactions and important details so you remember what happened</li>
    <li><strong>Use search during calls</strong> – When someone calls, quickly search to find their lead record</li>
    <li><strong>Review regularly</strong> – Check the board periodically to see what needs follow-up</li>
    <li><strong>Convert promptly</strong> – When a lead becomes a client, convert them so you can start managing them as a client</li>
</ul>

